<title>USA: Fannie Mae sets $250 mln REMIC 1997-06.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae sets $250 mln REMIC 1997-06.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal National Mortgage Association (Fannie Mae or FNMA) said it issued $250 million of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities.</p>
<p>REMIC trust 1997-06, issued via Credit Suisse First Boston, is backed by 30-year 7.0 percent mortgage-backed securities, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>The issue has a weighted average coupon of 7.6 percent, a weighted average maturity of 344 months, a pricing date of January 9 and a settlement date of January 30, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660))</p>
